menu "CAN TCP interfaces"
	depends on NET

config CAN_TCP_SLCAN
	tristate "Serial line CAN over TCP"
	depends on STREAM_PARSER
	help
	  This driver creates a standard SocketCAN network interface (canX)
	  that communicates using the ASCII SLCAN protocol. Unlike the
	  standard slcan driver that attaches to a TTY/Serial port, this
	  driver utilizes a TCP socket passed from userspace via ioctl.

	  It uses the kernel's strparser (Stream Parser) for efficient
	  message framing in kernel space.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called tcp_slcan.

endmenu
